set.body:
Add LDA as a new method on the unified core, proving the row-relation pullback generalizes beyond GPCA.

Build class-incidence row relations and construct between/within scatter only through:
S_B = secondOrder(X, L_B, X)
S_W = secondOrder(X, L_W, X).

Provide distinct programs:
- Fisher generalized Rayleigh-Ritz with an explicit within-scatter normalization operator;
- trace-ratio LDA with a separate geometric normalization.

Statistical shrinkage of S_W is not implemented as weight ridge. Until the operator-policy follow-on lands, accept only an already-certified realized within-scatter operator or a narrowly explicit fixed policy seam.

Acceptance:
- builders return OperatorProgram and fits return the generic certified fit plus discriminant scores;
- independent parity fixture against an R reference with documented conventions and tolerance;
- analytic two-class and rank-deficient fixtures;
- permutation, class-label relabeling, scale, subspace, and repeated-eigenvalue metamorphic tests;
- no LDA-specific solver engine; JVM and JS green.
